  "unit": "where-when",
  "title": "Out and In: ex-, e-, in- and en-",
  "short": "ex- and e- mean out; in-, im-, en- and em- mean in or into.",
  "trouble": "ex- shrinks to e- before many consonants (elicit, evasive, eminent) and becomes ef- before f (effrontery). The in- that means into is a different prefix from the in- that means not.",
  "prereqs": [
    "roots.pre-post"
  ],
  "xp": 1,
  "viz": [
    "vo-roots",
    "vo-word"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "practice": null,
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "An <i>exit</i> is the way out, and to <i>export</i> is to carry out of a country. <b>ex-</b> means “out.” Its opposite, <b>in-</b> (also <b>im-</b>, <b>en-</b>, <b>em-</b>), means “in” or “into”: to <i>inhale</i> is to breathe in, and to <i>enclose</i> is to shut in. A cousin, <b>extra-</b>, means “outside” or “beyond” (<i>extraordinary</i>)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-scene",
        "opts": {
          "scene": {
            "bg": "garden",
            "cast": [
              {
                "who": "greta",
                "x": 44,
                "s": 1.1,
                "pose": "pull",
                "holds": "carrot",
                "hsize": 1.8,
                "mood": "determined",
                "face": "right",
                "wear": [
                  "strawhat"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "fx": [
              {
                "kind": "dust",
                "x": 66,
                "y": 4
              },
              {
                "kind": "sweat",
                "on": "c0",
                "at": "head"
              }
            ],
            "labels": [
              {
                "text": "E + RADIC = ROOT OUT",
                "x": 50,
                "y": 92
              }
            ],
            "alt": "A gardener pulls a big carrot, a root, out of the ground."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A gardener pulls a big carrot, a root, out of the ground."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>ex-</b> = <b>out</b> (shortened to <b>e-</b> before many consonants and <b>ef-</b> before <i>f</i>). <b>in-</b>, <b>im-</b>, <b>en-</b>, <b>em-</b> = <b>in, into</b>. <b>extra-</b> = <b>outside, beyond</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "The pair <b>expedite</b> and <b>impede</b> shows the two at work on one root, <b>ped</b> (foot). To <i>expedite</i> is to free the feet (to get things moving faster); to <i>impede</i> is to catch the feet, as in a trap (to slow things down)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "ex",
          "words": [
            "exonerate",
            "expedite",
            "eradicate",
            "elucidate",
            "evasive",
            "eloquent",
            "exhort",
            "exalt",
            "extol",
            "effrontery"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on ex- and its shapes e- and ef-."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "in-into",
            "extra"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "in-, en- (into) and extra- (outside)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>exonerate</b><br>to clear from blame",
            "<b>ex-</b> <i>out</i> + oner <i>burden</i> + -ate<br>→ “take the burden off”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>expedite</b><br>to speed up",
            "<b>ex-</b> <i>out</i> + ped <i>foot</i> + -ite<br>→ “free the feet”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>eradicate</b><br>to destroy completely",
            "<b>e-</b> <i>out</i> + radic <i>root</i> + -ate<br>→ “pull out by the root”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>elucidate</b><br>to make clear; to explain",
            "<b>e-</b> <i>out</i> + lucid <i>bright</i> + -ate<br>→ “bring out into the light”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>evasive</b><br>avoiding a direct answer",
            "<b>e-</b> <i>out</i> + vas <i>go</i> + -ive<br>→ “going out of the way”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>extraneous</b><br>not relevant; coming from outside",
            "<b>extra</b> <i>outside</i> + -neous<br>→ “from outside”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>inundate</b><br>to flood; to overwhelm",
            "<b>in-</b> <i>into</i> + und <i>wave</i> + -ate<br>→ “send waves into”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>innate</b><br>present from birth; natural",
            "<b>in-</b> <i>in</i> + nat <i>born</i><br>→ “born in”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>impede</b><br>to delay or block",
            "<b>im-</b> <i>in</i> + ped <i>foot</i><br>→ “catch the feet”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>envision</b><br>to picture something in the mind, especially a future possibility",
            "<b>en-</b> <i>in</i> + vis <i>see</i> + -ion<br>→ “see in the mind”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The town hoped to <b>eradicate</b> the weeds that had taken over the park. What does <i>eradicate</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>e-</b> (out) + <b>radic</b> (root, as in <i>radish</i>) + <b>-ate</b> (verb ending).",
          "Literally: “to pull out by the root.”",
          "Pulling weeds out by the root gets rid of them for good."
        ],
        "a": "To destroy completely."
      },
