      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Missing <b>ex-</b> when it shrinks. It is <b>e-</b> in <i>elicit</i>, <i>evasive</i>, <i>eminent</i> and <i>edict</i>, and <b>ef-</b> in <i>effrontery</i>. And keep two different <b>in-</b>s apart: the one in this lesson means “into” (<i>innate</i>, <i>inundate</i>); the one that means “not” is a different prefix (<i>inept</i>, <i>insatiable</i>)."
